    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, why do snakes shed their skin?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🐍",
          "label": "Snake"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "✨",
          "label": "New skin?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A snake's outer skin doesn't stretch. So as the snake grows bigger, its skin gets too tight.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐍",
        "text": "Skin gets too tight",
        "cue": "tight",
        "sub": "The snake keeps growing",
        "sub_cue": "grows"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Like when my shoes get too small?",
      "punch": "shoes"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Exactly! So the snake grows a fresh new skin underneath, and wiggles out of the old one.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "✨",
        "text": "Fresh skin underneath",
        "cue": "fresh",
        "sub": "Wiggle out of the old",
        "sub_cue": "wiggles"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How does it get out?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "It rubs its nose on a rock to loosen the old skin. Then it crawls forward and slides out, like pulling off a sock!",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Out of old skin",
        "traveler": "🐍",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🪨",
            "label": "Rub nose",
            "cue": "rubs"
          },
          {
            "icon": "➡️",
            "label": "Crawl forward",
            "cue": "crawls"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧦",
            "label": "Slide out",
            "cue": "slides"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does the old skin come off in pieces?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Often it comes off in one long piece, inside out, with the pattern of every scale!",
      "punch": "inside",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐍",
        "text": "One long piece!",
        "cue": "piece",
        "sub": "Inside out",
        "sub_cue": "inside"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does a snake know when it's time?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Before shedding, its eyes turn cloudy and bluish, because even its eyes get a new clear cover!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👀",
        "text": "Cloudy blue eyes",
        "cue": "cloudy",
        "sub": "Eye covers shed too!",
        "sub_cue": "cover"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do we shed skin too?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "We do! But we shed tiny flakes all the time, so we never notice. Snakes do it all at once.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "You",
